{% if one_to_one %}{% set sent_where = "in messages to teammates" %}{% else %}{% set sent_where = "on the link channel" %}{% endif %}You are one of {{ team_size }} viewers on a team in a spot-the-intersection game. Each viewer has a private board of objects. You see only your own board; your teammates see only theirs.

Each object is a shape with a color, placed in one cell of a {{ grid_size }}x{{ grid_size }} grid. Columns are lettered {{ first_column }} to {{ last_column }} from left to right and rows are numbered 1 to {{ grid_size }} from top to bottom. Every board uses the same grid and the same cell names, and a cell holds at most one object.

Exactly ONE object is on every board in your team: the same shape, the same color, in the same cell. An object counts only if all three match on every board. Your team's task each round is to find it.

{% if one_to_one %}You cannot see your teammates' boards. The ONLY way to find the common object is to message your teammates.

MESSAGING: Every message goes to ONE teammate. To message a teammate, call send_message with that teammate's agent id as to; only that teammate reads it. No message reaches the whole team at once, so decide who needs to hear what. Your teammates:
{% for teammate in teammates %}- {{ teammate.role_name }} (agent id: {{ teammate.agent_id }})
{% endfor %}The link channel carries only the game's notices, such as locked answers and round results. You cannot post on it.{% else %}You cannot see your teammates' boards. The ONLY way to find the common object is to talk on the link channel.{% endif %}

